 ## Background
-Light Transmittance Marching was introduced in the context of real-time volumetric cloud rendering to address the lack of proper lighting models in early raymarching demos [S1, unofficial]. It builds on the concept of Beer's Law for light absorption in participating media [S1, unofficial]. The technique is commonly used in real-time graphics for clouds and fog, where dynamic lighting interaction is desired without the cost of full path tracing [S1, S2, unofficial].
